(1543,0,0,'The %s is ready to be captured!',16,0,100,0,0,0,'Vile Fin Puddlejumper'),
(1544,0,0,'The %s is ready to be captured!',16,0,100,0,0,0,'Vile Fin Minor Oracle'),
(1568,0,0,'Let\'s see, I just saw a corpse with a jaw that would fit you...',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Undertaker Mordo'),
(1568,1,0,'That should do the job. Come back right away if it falls off again.',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Undertaker Mordo'),
(1569,0,0,'Well, look who\'s here!',12,0,100,5,0,0,'Shadow Priest Sarvis'),
(1776,0,0,'Yes...',12,0,100,0,0,0,''),
(2055,0,0,'I assure you, overseer, the Royal Apothecary Society dearly wishes to make up for the tragic misguidance which ended so many lives.',12,1,100,0,0,0,'Master Apothecary Faranell '),
(2055,1,0,'We will cause you no trouble. We seek only to continue our research in peace.',12,1,100,0,0,0,'Master Apothecary Faranell '),
(2057,0,0,'I appreciate your help in this. We never would have suspected Saean as a sympathizer - we just weren\'t prepared for this.',12,7,100,0,0,0,'Huldar'),
(2057,1,0,'Good work! I\'m glad to see some revenge taken on that traitor. Go ahead and take the path Miran did to the east and let Prospector Ironband know we\'re all set. I\'m sure he\'ll have some work for you as well.',12,7,100,0,0,0,'Huldar'),
(2108,0,0,'Your bones will break under my boot, $r!',12,1,100,0,0,0,'Garneg Charskull'),
(2108,0,1,'Long live the Dragonmaw! Die you worthless $r!',12,1,100,0,0,0,'Garneg Charskull'),
(2108,0,2,'For the Dragonmaw!',12,1,100,0,0,0,'Garneg Charskull'),
(2120,0,0,'Destroy Arcane Fiends near Archmage Ataeric to overload the shield!',42,0,100,0,0,0,''),
(2120,1,0,'Minions, destroy the interloper! The shield must not come down!',14,0,100,0,0,0,''),
(2120,2,0,'You will not succeed, monster!',14,0,100,0,0,0,''),
(2120,3,0,'We will... never... give up!',14,0,100,0,0,0,''),
(2120,4,0,'The armies of the Alliance will march upon your bones!',14,0,100,0,0,0,''),
(2120,5,0,'Lordaeron belongs to the Alliance. You only delay the inevitable...',14,0,100,0,0,0,''),
(2120,6,0,'The power...is too much...I cannot hold...any longer...',14,0,100,0,0,0,''),
(2120,7,0,'RUN! DO NOT LET THEM TURN YOU!',14,0,100,0,0,0,''),
(2487,0,0,'Hey Baron, go long!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Fleet Master Seahorn'),
(2487,1,0,'That\'ll do.',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Fleet Master Seahorn'),
(2487,2,0,'Bring that back up to Yancey, by the waterfall.  The ignorant human\'ll have no idea that it\'s not me.',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Fleet Master Seahorn'),
(2501,0,0,'Alright, let\'s try cracking this thing open!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'"Sea Wolf" MacKinley'),
(2501,1,0,'%s tries opening Maury\'s Clubbed Foot...',16,0,100,0,0,0,'"Sea Wolf" MacKinley'),
(2501,2,0,'Aha!  It opened!  I expected that to be harder.  Thanks for your help, $n!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'"Sea Wolf" MacKinley'),
(2530,0,0,'Zanzil is creating an army that will wash over all of Stranglethorn!  Bloodscalps, Skullsplitter, Gurubashi and Horde... all will serve Zanzil!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Yenniku'),
(2530,1,0,'%s is struck dumb by the Soul Gem!',16,0,100,0,0,0,'Yenniku'),
(2532,0,0,'Ha ha! I have your Grindgear Gorilla!',12,7,100,0,0,0,'Donna'),
(2532,0,1,'I wonder if your Grindgear Gorilla can jump across the Park!',12,7,100,0,0,0,'Donna'),
(2532,0,2,'I have your gorilla! Nyah nyah!',12,7,100,0,0,0,'Donna'),
(2532,0,3,'I wonder how far the gears turn?',12,7,100,0,0,0,'Donna'),
(2532,0,4,'If you want him back you\'re gonna have to beg... like a monkey!!',12,7,100,0,0,0,'Donna'),
(2532,0,5,'Now who\'s the crybaby, crybaby!?',12,7,100,0,0,0,'Donna'),
(2532,0,6,'Baby wants his dolly!',12,7,100,0,0,0,'Donna'),
(2532,0,7,'Whoops!',12,7,100,0,0,0,'Donna'),
(2533,0,0,'No fair! Gimme back my gorilla!!',12,7,100,0,0,0,'William'),
(2533,0,1,'Gimmie back Jum-jump!',12,7,100,0,0,0,'William'),
(2533,0,2,'You better not break Jum-jump! It\'s not fair!',12,7,100,0,0,0,'William'),
(2533,0,3,'WAAAHHH!!!',12,7,100,0,0,0,'William'),
(2533,0,4,'You\'re being mean! I\'m telling Mommy!',12,7,100,0,0,0,'William'),
(2533,0,5,'Stop twisting his legs, they aren\'t supposed to bend that way!',12,7,100,0,0,0,'William'),
(2533,0,6,'You\'re breaking him!',12,7,100,0,0,0,'William'),
(2533,0,7,'Stop it! You\'ll break his legs off!',12,7,100,0,0,0,'William'),
(2545,0,0,'This is humiliating.',12,0,100,18,0,0,''),
(2545,1,0,'I can\'t believe it\'s come to this.',12,0,100,38,0,0,''),
(2545,2,0,'A mop?  Really?',12,0,100,38,0,0,''),
(2545,3,0,'I suppose sometimes y\'need to hit rock bottom before y\'can crawl yer way back up.',12,0,100,38,0,0,''),
(2545,4,0,'Maybe I need a new nickname.',12,0,100,6,0,0,''),
(2597,0,0,'I presume you come with good news?',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Lord Falconcrest'),
(2599,0,0,'Things are going as planned, Lord Falconcrest. I assure you, it is only a matter of time.',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Otto'),
(2663,0,0,'Tell him this is the last one.  It breaks poor Narkk\'s heart to have to carve horn-holes in his beautiful hats!',12,0,100,18,0,0,'Narkk'),
(2918,1,0,'This was my fault, my lord. I should\'ve done more research on those tablets...',12,0,100,6,0,0,'Children\'s Week - Quest: The Biggest Diamond Ever'),
(3511,0,0,'Why do we have to learn this stuff anyway?',12,7,100,1,0,0,'Steven'),
(3512,0,0,'Is it true that the paladins train here?',12,7,100,1,0,0,'Jimmy'),
(3513,0,0,'Here we have the Cathedral of Light, the center of spiritual enlightenment here in Stormwind.',12,7,100,1,0,0,'Miss Danna'),
(3513,1,0,'Yes, that is true. Paladins and Priests alike train their skills and research great truths behind the walls of the Cathedral.',12,7,100,1,0,0,'Miss Danna'),
(3513,2,0,'Children if you would please follow me, we will now be going to see the keep where King Anduin Wrynn himself sits on his throne.',12,7,100,1,0,0,'Miss Danna'),
(3513,3,0,'Here we have Stormwind Keep. Built upon the ruins of Stormwind Castle, which was destroyed by the Horde in the first Great War.',12,7,100,0,0,0,'Miss Danna'),
(3513,4,0,'When the Horde was shattered, men returned here and began to rebuild the once great city as a testament to our own survival.',12,7,100,0,0,0,'Miss Danna'),
(3513,5,0,'Yes, well...let\'s head on to the monument dedicated to the heroes of the two Great Wars, the Valley of Heroes. Follow Me.',12,7,100,1,0,0,'Miss Danna'),
(3513,6,0,'Isn\'t it amazing, children? All who enter the city must walk beneath the watchful eyes of the greatest heroes of our lands.',12,7,100,0,0,0,'Miss Danna'),
(3513,7,0,'Breathtaking. Children, when we return to the school, you will each give an oral report on one of these legendary people.',12,7,100,0,0,0,'Miss Danna'),
(3513,8,0,'Now, take another long look before we make our way to the Holy District and the great Cathedral of Light.',12,7,100,1,0,0,'Miss Danna'),
(3937,0,0,'Fresh bread, baked this very morning!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Kira Songshine'),
(3937,0,1,'Come get yer fresh bread!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Kira Songshine'),
(3937,0,2,'Fresh bread for sale!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Kira Songshine'),
(3937,1,0,'Guards! Help me!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Kira Songshine'),
(3946,0,0,'The numbers of my companions dwindles, goddess, and my own power shall soon be insufficient to hold back the demons of Felwood.',12,7,100,1,0,0,'Velinde Starsong'),
(3946,1,0,'Goddess, grant me the power to overcome my enemies! Hear me, please, my need is desperate and my cause is just!',12,7,100,1,0,0,'Velinde Starsong'),
(3946,2,0,'What... what is this? Could this be the answer to my prayers? Elune has granted me a weapon--this scythe--to defeat the demons.',12,7,100,1,0,0,'Velinde Starsong'),
(4607,0,0,'Ugh! What is that scoundrel doing sending his vermin to me? Get out of my sight before I take what is left of your life. And take this with you.',12,33,100,1,0,0,'Father Lankester'),
(4851,0,0,'%s goes into a frenzy!',16,0,100,0,0,0,'Stonevault Rockchewer'),
(5159,0,0,'There ye are! I was startin\' to think ye\'d made off with the beer!',12,0,100,5,0,0,''),
(5661,0,0,'Edward. Tyler. Prepare for your first challenge.',12,33,100,1,0,0,'Brother Malach'),
(5661,1,0,'Lysta, summon in the captives.',12,33,100,0,0,0,'Brother Malach'),
(5661,2,0,'Not a challenge at all it seems. Let us see how you handle your second test. Lysta, bring forth the minions of the Lich King.',12,33,100,0,0,0,'Brother Malach'),
(5661,3,0,'Lysta, summon in undead captives.',12,33,100,0,0,0,'Brother Malach'),
(5661,4,0,'It is time to face your final challenge young warriors! Prepare for your hardest fight yet.',12,33,100,0,0,0,'Brother Malach'),
(5661,5,0,'Lysta, summon forth... the abomination!',12,33,100,0,0,0,'Brother Malach'),
(5661,6,0,'Well done Edward and Tyler. You are progressing along in your training quite nicely. We shall test your mettle again soon.',12,33,100,0,0,0,'Brother Malach'),
(5662,0,0,'You sorry sacks of maggot flesh can do better than that, now prove it!',12,33,100,0,0,0,'Sergeant Houser'),
(5662,0,1,'Alright you sorry sacks of bones. Let\'s see what you\'ve got. Strike your opponent, and don\'t stop till I say so.',12,33,100,0,0,0,'Sergeant Houser'),
(5662,0,2,'What do you call that? If that\'s fighting then I\'m Lothar himself!',12,33,100,0,0,0,'Sergeant Houser'),
(5662,0,3,'These piles of wood and straw may show mercy, but the Lich King won\'t!',12,33,100,0,0,0,'Sergeant Houser'),
(5662,0,4,'The sword isn\'t a tool, it\'s an extension of you. I expect better!',12,33,100,0,0,0,'Sergeant Houser'),
(5662,0,5,'Stop! You maggots call that fighting? That is pathetic! Now put your hearts in it, you don\'t need them anymore anyway!',12,33,100,0,0,0,'Sergeant Houser'),
(5662,0,6,'You\'re dead, not buried. Now show me your best!',12,33,100,0,0,0,'Sergeant Houser'),
(5662,0,7,'You don\'t fight for yourselves anymore, maggots! You fight for the Queen now so show me something worthy of her!',12,33,100,0,0,0,'Sergeant Houser'),
(5696,0,0,'Theresa, take this to Father Lankester.',12,33,100,1,0,0,'Gerard Abernathy'),
(5696,1,0,'Why thank you, my pet.',12,33,100,1,0,0,'Gerard Abernathy'),
(5696,2,0,'As good as I told you it would be, yes?',12,33,100,1,0,0,'Gerard Abernathy'),
(5696,2,1,'Didn\'t I tell you my new domination techniques would work?',12,33,100,1,0,0,'Gerard Abernathy'),
(5696,2,2,'So what do you think of my new toy?',12,33,100,1,0,0,'Gerard Abernathy'),
(5696,2,3,'How do you like my pet?',12,33,100,1,0,0,'Gerard Abernathy'),
(5696,2,4,'Isn\'t she just the most amazing little creation?',12,33,100,1,0,0,'Gerard Abernathy'),
(5696,3,0,'A little torture, a pinch of magic, and an ample helping of invasive surgery. She was conscious, of course.',12,33,100,1,0,0,'Gerard Abernathy'),
(5696,3,1,'Everyone has a weakness, it\'s just a matter of finding it.',12,33,100,1,0,0,'Gerard Abernathy'),
(5696,3,2,'It was simple once I broke her spirit.',12,33,100,1,0,0,'Gerard Abernathy'),
(5696,3,3,'I managed to discover that certain parts of the brain when removed or stimulated will make a subject much more docile. ',12,33,100,1,0,0,'Gerard Abernathy'),
(5696,3,4,'You don\'t expect me to give up all my secrets do you?',12,33,100,1,0,0,'Gerard Abernathy'),
(5696,3,5,'A little ritual torture can go a long way.',12,33,100,1,0,0,'Gerard Abernathy'),
(5697,0,0,'Yes My Lord.',12,33,100,0,0,0,'Theresa'),
(5697,1,0,'My Lord Abernathy sends this to you.',12,33,100,0,0,0,'Theresa'),
(5697,2,0,'My Lord. From Father Lankester.',12,33,100,0,0,0,'Theresa'),
(5698,0,0,'Bravo, Gerard, you have exceeded yourself, yet again.',12,33,100,1,0,0,'Joanna Whitehall'),
(5698,0,1,'I am truly impressed, Gerard. I thought you were all talk, but I see I have been proven wrong.',12,33,100,1,0,0,'Joanna Whitehall'),
(5698,0,2,'I don\'t agree with your turning to alchemy to fix some of the problems, but I do agree with the results. Very well done.',12,33,100,0,0,0,'Joanna Whitehall'),
(5698,0,3,'Did you have to house train her, Gerard?',12,33,100,1,0,0,'Joanna Whitehall'),
(5698,0,4,'An amazing discovery you have made. I would love an opportunity to look at all of the failed experiments.',12,33,100,0,0,0,'Joanna Whitehall'),
(5698,0,6,'Very nice, Gerard. Next you will be breeding them.',12,33,100,1,0,0,'Joanna Whitehall'),
(5698,0,7,'Your pet is wonderful, Gerard, but she needs a collar with a bell I think.',12,33,100,1,0,0,'Joanna Whitehall'),
(5699,0,0,'I\'ve never seen anything like it. No concentration or loss of awareness while the subject is dominated. What did you do to her?',12,33,100,1,0,0,'Leona Tharpe'),
(5699,0,1,'Amazing! How did you manage a permanent dominate?',12,33,100,1,0,0,'Leona Tharpe'),
(5699,0,2,'I don\'t approve of your experiments, Gerard, but I must admit the results are impressive. What exactly did you do to her?',12,33,100,1,0,0,'Leona Tharpe'),
(5699,0,3,'She retains knowledge and speech, and even the self sufficiency to perform tasks for you. Precisely what did you do?',12,33,100,1,0,0,'Leona Tharpe'),
(5699,0,4,'Truly amazing, Gerard. How did you do it?',12,33,100,1,0,0,'Leona Tharpe'),
(5700,0,0,'If I could just find "Magic and the Ways of Power". Ahh here it is, what was it doing over here?',12,33,100,0,0,0,''),
(5700,0,1,'Very interesting. But if that\'s the case then my theory is wrong. I must reread the other sections to see what I missed.',12,33,100,0,0,0,''),
(5700,0,2,'"Magical Flows and How They Effect the World", by Maginor Dumas. That\'s the one I was looking for.',12,33,100,0,0,0,''),
(5700,0,3,'If this is correct then I have a lot more research to do.',12,33,100,0,0,0,''),
(5700,0,4,'Ahh there it is.',12,33,100,0,0,0,''),
(5700,0,5,'I really need a better system for filing these books. Ahh that\'s the one I wanted.',12,33,100,0,0,0,''),
(5700,0,6,'But this can\'t be right. Where did I put that other book?',12,33,100,0,0,0,''),
(5700,0,7,'"Khadgar\'s Mystical Journal, Volume 8." I think this is the one I wanted.',12,33,100,0,0,0,''),
(5700,0,8,'Ahh, "Mystical Conjurings of the Archmages of Dalaran." Perfect.',12,33,100,0,0,0,''),
(5700,0,9,'If I could just find "Magic and the Ways of Power". Ahh here it is, what was it doing over here?',12,33,100,0,0,0,''),
(5700,0,10,'"Magic Maladies", no. "Magic Matricies", no. Ahh here we go "Magic Mysteries".',12,33,100,0,0,0,''),
(5700,0,11,'There\'s the mystical tome I was looking for.',12,33,100,0,0,0,''),
(5700,0,12,'Yes, yes. Hmm, it seems to cross reference another tome. Guess I have to find that one too.',12,33,100,0,0,0,''),
(5700,0,13,'That wasn\'t very helpful. Let me check the other one.',12,33,100,0,0,0,''),
(5700,0,14,'That\'s what I wanted to know. Now I just need to find where the flux variance is discussed.',12,33,100,0,0,0,''),
(5700,0,15,'So I was right about the energies. Let\'s see what the other tome has to say on the subject.',12,33,100,0,0,0,''),
(5700,0,16,'Back to the drawing board.',12,33,100,0,0,0,''),
(5734,0,0,'Hmm, it would seem Keever needs a new subject. If that fool Abernathy keeps taking Keever\'s subjects, Keever may have to have a word with him.',12,33,100,1,0,0,'Apothecary Keever <Royal Apothecary Society>'),
